      "math_academy_id": "e-4449",
      "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14250940/assets/cf118a78f757b397bbaf7c0ebe1b72a59997c493fc84a46bbae7a2c4aaa8af6e.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+2\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2{C}_{13} \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 1 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & ∗ & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & ∗ & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(5|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =2(5(6\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3)-(1\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-6))+0(1\\cdot 3-6\\cdot (-6))) \\\\  & =2(15+6+0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$",
